{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_pgRZmyy1zzc3pKIeFM6Gl99u","content":"1\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-03 2x:xx +0700\n2\tCoding-Agent: kimi\n3\tSession: fresh (engineer round — P9)\n4\tWorktree: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-p9 (branch feat/p9-builtin-surfaces @ origin/master)\n5\t\n6\t# Task: P9 — builtin surface slices (yang.php.md section 15, the P9 row)\n7\t\n8\tScope: builtin surface slices (strings II, arrays II, JSON, math II), `$$` (variable variables), `extract`, `compact` and the dynamic scope, `eval` as a compilation request (section 3.12: eval shares the caller's symbol table).\n9\t\n10\tAlso in scope (the P9 row's corner closures): C5, C6 (prefer-ref), C11, C12, C13 — read their definitions in yang.php.md's corners section and implement/refuse each per the doc.\n11\t\n12\t## Method (the track's standing pattern)\n13\t\n14\t1. Read the P9 row, section 3.12 (eval), the corners section (C5, C6, C11, C12, C13), and the existing builtin structure (builtins.cljc, programs_p4/p5 patterns).\n15\t2. Implement the builtin groups in the prelude/runtime; author the corpus fixture groups (programs_p9.cljc, the fx pattern) with hand-derived expectations where PHP semantics are unambiguous; mark ambiguous ones :oracle :pending (the seat runs the recording pass).\n16\t3. `$$`, `extract`, `compact` need the dynamic-scope helper the doc mentions (section 16's optional `:dynamic-scope`) — check whether the helper exists; if the doc requires a design amendment first, write the amendment into yang.php.md as part of this round.\n17\t4. `eval` as a compilation request: eval'd code compiles through the same pipeline at run time and shares the caller's symbol table.\n18\t5. GATE: the new P9 fixture groups green on the JVM (bundled); the php consumers (class-model/objects/generators/request-context) stay green; kondo/cljstyle clean.\n19\t6. COMMIT on feat/p9-builtin-surfaces (feat(yang.php): P9 — the builtin surface slices), no Co-Authored-By. Do NOT push. Findings to collab/orch-lane/1794350000000-engineer-p9-builtin-surfaces.kimi-k3.1-pro.findings.md (uncommitted).\n20\t\n21\tScope discipline: this is a LARGE slice. If the window runs short, land the slices you completed with an honest findings report naming what remains — do not rush the rest."}
