 `array_push`,       | restricted; P2   |\n2216\t| by-reference        | `preg_match`'s `&$m`, prefer-ref    | (core), P9       |\n2217\t| parameters          | `array_multisort`, the \"Only        | (prefer-ref)     |\n2218\t|                     | variables should be passed by       |                  |\n2219\t|                     | reference\" notice. Here: each       |                  |\n2220\t|                     | supported builtin declares its      |                  |\n2221\t|                     | by-reference positions; the notice  |                  |\n2222\t|                     | is emitted; prefer-ref builtins are |                  |\n2223\t|                     | refused                             |                  |\n2224\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\n2225\t| C7 return by        | Engine: `function &f()`, `&__get`,  | unsupported; a   |\n2226\t| reference           | `&offsetGet`. Here: refused         | slice after P9   |\n2227\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\n2228\t| C8 generator        | Engine: destroying a suspended      | restricted; P4-c |\n2229\t| destruction         | generator runs its pending          |                  |\n2230\t|                     | `finally` blocks and releases its   |                  |\n2231\t|                     | frame. Here: its CVs are released   |                  |\n2232\t|                     | (rows 16, 39) but pending `finally` |                  |\n2233\t|                     | blocks do not run                   |                  |\n2234\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\n2235\t| C9                  | Engine: `Attempt to destruct        | restricted; none |\n2236\t| pending-exception   | pending exception`. Here: an        | planned          |\n2237\t| destruct fatal      | `Error`-class halt with pinned      |                  |\n2238\t|                     | text, not a process fatal           |                  |\n2239\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\n2240\t| C10 property hooks, | Engine: PHP 8.4. Here: not parsed   | unsupported; a   |\n2241\t| asymmetric          | (8.3 pinned)                        | grammar and      |\n2242\t| visibility          |                                     | version bump     |\n2243\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\n2244\t| C11 dynamic-scope   | Engine: `extract(EXTR_REFS)`,       | unsupported      |\n2245\t| references          | `compact` of references, `$$name =& | until P9         |\n2246\t|                     | ...`, `get_defined_vars`. Here: the |                  |\n2247\t|                     | symbol table holds markers like any |                  |\n2248\t|                     | location; `EXTR_REFS` and `$$x =&`  |                  |\n2249\t|                     | are refused                         |                  |\n2250\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\n2251\t| C12 nested          | Engine: `[[&$a]] = ...` and keyed   | restricted; P9   |\n2252\t| destructuring by    | nested forms. Here: one level (row  |                  |\n2253\t| reference           | 47); deeper refused                 |                  |\n2254\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\n2255\t| C13 `$GLOBALS`      | Engine: `$GLOBALS` is a read-only   | restricted; P9   |\n2256\t| write semantics     | copy, element writes allowed,       |                  |\n2257\t| (8.1)               | `$GLOBALS = ...` a compile error.   |                  |\n2258\t|                     | Here: element writes supported;     |                  |\n2259\t|                     | whole-array operations on           |                  |\n2260\t|                     | `$GLOBALS` refused                  |                