{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_nOCnmhsjRvB55FboNmgnSoo5","content":"1620\t+------------+--------------------------------+--------------------------------+\n1621\t\n1622\t## 9. The prelude inventory\n1623\t\n1624\tModule `php` (reserved), hook prelude `phpsp`. `php/init!` builds the class\n1625\ttable with the builtin classes and interfaces (`stdClass`, `Closure`,\n1626\t`Generator`, `Traversable`, `Iterator`, `IteratorAggregate`, `ArrayAccess`,\n1627\t`Countable`, `Stringable`, `JsonSerializable`, `UnitEnum`, `BackedEnum`, the\n1628\t`Throwable` hierarchy; `ArrayObject` deferred), the function table with the\n1629\tsupported builtins and their by-reference positions, `$GLOBALS` from the\n1630\trequest record, the output-buffer stack, the error-handler cell, the\n1631\tincluded-files dict, the `finalizable` registry and the shutdown-function\n1632\tlist, and flips `php.rt/state` to `:php/ready` last.\n1633\t\n1634\t+--------------------------+--------------------------------------+------------+\n1635\t| Area                     | Supported core (Phase 3)             | Est. lines |\n1636\t+==========================+======================================+============+\n1637\t| Type juggling            | `to-int`, `to-float`, `to-string`    | 700        |\n1638\t|                          | (precision 14), `to-bool`,           |            |\n1639\t|                          | `to-array`, numeric-string           |            |\n1640\t|                          | classification, the `==`/`<=>`/`===` |            |\n1641\t|                          | tables, `gettype`, `is_*`, `intval`, |            |\n1642\t|                          | `floatval`, `strval`, `boolval`,     |            |\n1643\t|                          | `settype`, and the `var_dump`,       |            |\n1644\t|                          | `print_r` and `var_export` text      |            |\n1645\t|                          | (serialize precision -1, the `#n`    |            |\n1646\t|                          | object ids, indentation rules)       |            |\n1647\t+--------------------------+--------------------------------------+------------+\n1648\t| Arrays                   | `count`; `array_keys`, `_values`,    | 900        |\n1649\t|                          | `_merge`, `_merge_recursive`,        |            |\n1650\t|                          | `_combine`, `_flip`, `_slice`,       |            |\n1651\t|                          | `_splice`, `_map`, `_filter`,        |            |\n1652\t|                          | `_reduce`, `_walk`, `_search`,       |            |\n1653\t|                          | `_key_exists`, `in_array`,           |            |\n1654\t|                          | `_unique`, `_reverse`, `_sum`,       |            |\n1655\t|                          | `_product`, `_fill`, `_fill_keys`,   |            |\n1656\t|                          | `_pad`, `_chunk`, `_column`,         |            |\n1657\t|                          | `_diff`/`_intersect` (with           |            |\n1658\t|                          | `_key`/`_assoc`), `_push`, `_pop`,   |            |\n1659\t|                          | `_shift`, `_unshift`, `_key_first`,  |            |\n1660\t|                          | `_key_last`, `_is_list`; the sort    |            |\n1661\t|                          | family (stable since 8.0, a flags    |            |\n1662\t|                          | subset); `range`; `compact` and      |            |\n1663\t|                          | `extract` (dynamic profile);         |            |\n1664\t|                          | `implode`, `explode`, `str_split`;   |            |\n1665\t|                          | `iterator_to_array`; `current`,      |            |\n1666\t|                          | `key`, `next`, `reset`, `end`,       |            |\n1667\t|                          | `prev` (row 55)                      |            |\n1668\t+--------------------------+--------------------------------------+------------+\n1669\t| Strings (byte strings)   | `strlen`, `substr`,                  | 900        |\n1670\t|                          | `strpos`/`stripos`/`strrpos`,        |            |\n1671\t|                          | `str_replace`/`str_ireplace`,        |            |\n1672\t|                          | `str_contains`, `str_starts_with`,   |            |\n1673\t|                          | `str_ends_with`,                     |            |\n1674\t|                          | `trim`/`ltrim`/`rtrim`, ASCII        |            |\n1675\t|                          | case functions (PHP 8 is             |            |\n1676\t|                          | locale-insensitive), `str_repeat`,   |            |\n1677\t|                          | `str_pad`, `strrev`, `strcmp`,       |            |\n1678\t|                          | `strcasecmp`, `strncmp`, `strstr`,   |            |\n1679\t|                          | `strrchr`, `substr_count`,           |            |\n1680\t|                          | `wordwrap`, `nl2br`,                 |            |\n1681\t|                          | `htmlspecialchars`, basic            |            |\n1682\t|                          | `html_entity_decode`, `addslashes`,  |            |\n1683\t|                          | `stripslashes`, `chunk_split`,       |            |\n1684\t|                          | `sprintf`, `printf`, `vsprintf`,     |            |\n1685\t|                          | `number_format`, `ord`, `chr`,       |            |\n1686\t|                          | `bin2hex`,                           |            |\n1687\t|                          | `hex2bin`, base conversions; `md5`,  |            |\n1688\t|                          | `sha1`, `crc32`, `hash('sha256')`    |            |\n1689\t|                          | only where pure kernels exist, else  |            |\n1690\t|                          | refused; `json_encode`/`json_decode` |            |\n1691\t|                          | (a flags subset,                     |            |\n1692\t|                          | `JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR`, pretty        |            |\n1693\t|                          | print); `serialize` deferred;        |            |\n1694\t|                          | `preg_*` refused                     |            |\n1695\t+--------------------------+--------------------------------------+------------+\n1696\t| Math                     | `abs`, `ceil`, `floor`, `round`      | 250        |\n1697\t|                          | (PHP's pre-rounding rule), `intdiv`, |            |\n1698\t|                          | `fmod`, `pow`, `sqrt`, `min`, `max`, |            |\n1699\t|                          | `array_sum`;                         |            |\n1700\t|                          | `PHP_INT_MAX`/`MIN`/`SIZE`,          |            |\n1701\t|                          | `PHP_FLOAT_*`, `M_PI`; `is_nan`,     |            |\n1702\t|                          | `is_finite`, `is_infinite`; `rand`,  |            |\n1703\t|                          | `mt_rand`, `random_int` as effects   |            |\n1704\t+--------------------------+--------------------------------------+------------+\n1705\t| Functions and classes    | call binding (positional, named,     | 700        |\n1706\t|                          | variadic, by-reference, defaults,    |            |\n1707\t|                          | coercion and `TypeError`,            |            |\n1708\t|                          | `ArgumentCountError`) through        |            |\n1709\t|                          | pending calls; `func_get_args`,      |            |\n1710\t|                          | `call_user_func(_array)`,            |            |\n1711\t|                          | `is_callable`, `function_exists`;    |            |\n1712\t|                          | class-table operations, `get_class`, |            |\n1713\t|                          | `get_parent_class`, `method_exists`, |            |\n1714\t|                          | `property_exists`, `class_exists`,   |            |\n1715\t|                          | `get_object_vars`, `spl_object_id`;  |            |\n1716\t|                          | visibility checks; magic dispatch;   |            |\n1717\t|                          | `Closure::bind`, `fromCallable` and  |            |\n1718\t|                          | `call`; enum                         |            |\n1719\t|                          | `cases`/`from`/`tryFrom`;            |            |\n1720\t|                          | object `:rc`, finalization and       |            |\n1721\t|                          | `clone` (section 4.4.6)              |            |\n1722\t+--------------------------+--------------------------------------+------------+\n1723\t| Control and errors       | the handler stack (the Python        | 350        |\n1724\t|                          | pattern), `php/raise`, `finally`,    |            |\n1725\t|                          | escapes with levels, `RELEASE_CVS`   |            |\n1726\t|                          | and temp-list release; `Throwable`   |            |\n1727\t|                          | classes with `getMessage`,           |            |\n1728\t|                          | `getCode`, `getPrevious`, `getTrace` |            |\n1729\t|                          | (empty; C30), `getLine` (derived at  |            |\n1730\t|                          | the boundary); `set_error_handler`,  |            |\n1731\t|                          | `restore_error_handler`,             |            |\n1732\t|                          | `set_exception_handler`,             |            |\n1733\t|                          | `trigger_error`, `error_reporting`;  |            |\n1734\t|                          | warning emission `php/warn`          |            |\n1735\t+--------------------------+--------------------------------------+------------+\n1736\t| Generators and iteration | the C2 core under `php/`, the        | 300        |\n1737\t|                          | `Iterator` protocol, the `foreach`   |            |\n1738\t|                          | driver with iterators (section       |            |\n1739\t|                          | 4.4.3), `yield from` over arrays and |            |\n1740\t|                          | generators                           |            |\n1741\t+--------------------------+--------------------------------------+------------+\n1742\t| Request and output       | `$_*` construction, `php/echo`, the  | 300        |\n1743\t|                          | `ob_*` stack, `header`,              |            |\n1744\t|                          | `headers_sent`,                      |            |\n1745\t|                          | `http_response_code`, `setcookie`,   |            |\n1746\t|                          | `exit`, `register_shutdown_function` |            |\n1747\t|                          | and the shutdown sequence (row 22),  |            |\n1748\t|                          | `php_sapi_name` (`\"cli\"` or          |            |\n1749\t|                          | `\"yin-http\"`, pinned), `getenv` from |            |\n1750\t|                          | the record only, `PHP_EOL`, a pinned |            |\n1751\t|                          | `PHP_VERSION`, `error_log` as an     |            |\n1752\t|                          | effect                               |            |\n1753\t+--------------------------+--------------------------------------+------------+\n1754\t| Module runtime           | `include`, `require`, `_once`, the   | 250        |\n1755\t|                          | included-files dict, the autoload    |            |\n1756\t|                          | class map, `define`, `constant`,     |            |\n1757\t|                          | `defined`, namespace lookup          |            |\n1758\t+--------------------------+--------------------------------------+------------+\n1759\t\n1760\tRefusal posture: a builtin outside the supported core is\n1761\t`:yang.php/unknown-builtin` at lowering (a warning) and `Error: Call to\n1762\tundefined function` at run time; an extension surface is bound per ADR 0004 as\n1763\tits own slice with an effect schema and an interpreter; nothing is stubbed to\n1764\treturn success. Until the `yrt` shared prelude is scheduled\n1765\t(`yang.typescript.md` owner decision A12.5), PHP copies the escape machinery,\n1766\tgenerator core, ordered map and module skeleton patterns under `php/`; it\n1767\twould be `yrt`'s second consumer.\n1768\t\n1769\t## 10. Value encoding and paradigm-table rows\n1770\t\n1771\t### 10.1 Value encoding (runtime profile data)\n1772\t\n1773\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\n1774\t| PHP type        | Representation                                             |\n1775\t+=================+============================================================+\n1776\t| int             | exact integer within `[-2^63, 2^63-1]` (C3 carriers; on    |\n1777\t|                 | the JavaScript host a value past 2^53 is a `BigInt`        |\n1778\t|                 | carrier); an operation's overflow demotes to float         |\n1779\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\n1780\t| float           | Jing float64 content (carrier on the JavaScript host); one |\n1781\t|                 | NaN; `-0.0` preserved; `INF`                               |\n1782\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\n1783\t| string          | **byte string**: a host string whose every char is one     |\n1784\t|                 | byte 0 to 255 (a latin-1 carrier of the bytes); source     |\n1785\t|                 | literals contribute their UTF-8 bytes; `strlen` counts     |\n1786\t|                 | bytes; output writes the bytes raw; `mb_*` is a separate   |\n1787\t|                 | slice over this representation (owner decision B8.2)       |\n1788\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\n1789\t| bool            | host boolean                                               |\n1790\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\n1791\t| null            | `:php/null`                                                |\n1792\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\n1793\t| array, plain    | `{:php/type :array :index {key slot} :order [key ...]      |\n1794\t|                 | :next-index n}` stored directly in its holder (section     |\n1795\t|                 | 4.2); `:next-index` is absent until the first integer key  |\n1796\t|                 | is written                                                 |\n1797\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\n1798\t| array, instance | cell `{:php/type :arr :rc n :value <plain map> :deps       |\n1799\t|                 | #{keys} :iterators #{it} :ptr i}`, held through `{:php/arr |\n1800\t|                 | h}`                                                        |\n1801\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\n1802\t| reference       | cell `{:php/type :ref :rc n :value x :sources #{[o p]}}`,  |\n1803\t|                 | held through the marker `{:php/ref c}` in a variable,      |\n1804\t|                 | property or instance slot                                  |\n1805\t+-----------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\n1806\t| object          | cell `{:php/type :obj :rc n :class C :props ordered-map    |\n1807\t|                 | :ord n :destructed? b}` with per-property `initialized?`   |\n1808\t|                 | and `reinitable` state; `:ord` is the per-task creation    |\n1809\t|                 | ordinal, also the `#n` of `var_dump` and `spl_object_id`   |"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_PeOst5rVp43EJgkNh9gmYdVa","content":"1\t(ns yang.php.antlr.programs-p4\n2\t  \"Slice P4 Stage 0 (S0) fixture data: classes, exceptions, constructors and\n3\t   readonly groups (P4 plan v2, S0). Same schema as\n4\t   `yang.php.antlr.programs-p3b`; `:oracle` is `:pending` until a recording is\n5\t   folded, and `:requires` names the P4 steps (:p4-s1 .. :p4-s12) that must land\n6\t   before an implementation runner may execute it. A recorded result is\n7\t   authoritative and replaces any hand-authored output pin.\n8\t\n9\t   `all-fixtures` is unconditional (the oracle iterates it). `enabled` is the\n10\t   subset whose :requires have all landed in `completed-steps`.\"\n11\t  (:require\n12\t    [clojure.string]\n13\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p3b :as p3b]))\n14\t\n15\t\n16\t(def completed-steps\n17\t  \"P4 steps that have landed. A fixture whose :requires name a later step\n18\t   stays disabled.\"\n19\t  #{:p4-s1 :p4-s2 :p4-s3 :p4-s4 :p4-s5 :p4-s6 :p4-s8})\n20\t\n21\t\n22\t(defn- fx\n23\t  ([id group rows requires source out]\n24\t   (fx id group rows requires source out :program))\n25\t  ([id group rows requires source out level]\n26\t   (cond-> {:id id,\n27\t            :group group,\n28\t            :rows rows,\n29\t            :level level,\n30\t            :requires requires,\n31\t            :source source,\n32\t            :oracle :pending}\n33\t     out (assoc :out out))))\n34\t\n35\t\n36\t(def classes-v1\n37\t  [(fx :cls-new-and-method :classes-v1 [] #{:p4-s2}\n38\t       \"<?php class A { public $x = 1; function get() { return $this->x; } } $a = new A; echo $a->get();\"\n39\t       \"1\")\n40\t   (fx :cls-static-prop-shared :classes-v1 [] #{:p4-s2}\n41\t       \"<?php class A { public static $n = 0; } class B extends A {} A::$n++; B::$n++; echo A::$n, B::$n;\"\n42\t       \"22\")\n43\t   (fx :cls-static-prop-redeclared-unshared :classes-v1 [] #{:p4-s2}\n44\t       \"<?php class A { public static $n = 0; } class B extends