{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_1jN8KDmdodN1mRhig5ww58Pk","content":"1\t(ns yang.php.antlr.programs-p5\n2\t  \"P5 request-context fixtures. Expectations are hand-derived from PHP 8.3;\n3\t  every fixture remains available to the oracle recording pass.\")\n4\t\n5\t\n6\t(defn request-array\n7\t  [entries]\n8\t  {:php/type :array, :index (into {} entries), :order (mapv first entries)})\n9\t\n10\t\n11\t(def request\n12\t  {:php.request/method \"POST\"\n13\t   :php.request/uri \"/hello?a=1\"\n14\t   :php.request/query (request-array [[\"a\" \"1\"] [\"shared\" \"get\"]])\n15\t   :php.request/headers (request-array [[\"X-Test\" \"yes\"]])\n16\t   :php.request/cookies (request-array [[\"session\" \"abc\"]])\n17\t   :php.request/body (request-array [[\"b\" \"2\"] [\"shared\" \"post\"]])\n18\t   :php.request/server (request-array [[\"SERVER_NAME\" \"fixture.test\"]])\n19\t   :php.request/env (request-array [[\"APP_ENV\" \"test\"]])\n20\t   :php.request/files (request-array [[\"upload\" \"fixture\"]])})\n21\t\n22\t\n23\t(defn- fx\n24\t  [id source out & {:as more}]\n25\t  (merge {:id id, :group :request-context, :source source, :out out,\n26\t          :request request, :oracle :pending}\n27\t         more))\n28\t\n29\t\n30\t(def fixtures\n31\t  [(fx :superglobals-from-request\n32\t       (str \"<?php echo $_GET['a'], $_POST['b'], $_COOKIE['session'],\"\n33\t            \" $_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'], $_SERVER['REQUEST_URI'],\"\n34\t            \" $_SERVER['SERVER_NAME'], $_ENV['APP_ENV'], $_FILES['upload'],\"\n35\t            \" $_REQUEST['a'], $_REQUEST['b'], $_REQUEST['shared'];\")\n36\t       \"12abcPOST/hello?a=1fixture.testtestfixture12post\")\n37\t   (fx :output-buffering\n38\t       \"<?php ob_start(); echo 'a'; echo ob_get_contents(); ob_start(); echo 'b'; echo ob_get_clean(); echo ob_get_clean(); echo 'c';\"\n39\t       \"aabc\")\n40\t   (fx :output-buffer-flush\n41\t       \"<?php ob_start(); echo 'a'; ob_end_flush(); echo 'b'; var_dump(ob_end_clean());\"\n42\t       \"abbool(false)\\n\")\n43\t   (fx :headers-cookies-status\n44\t       \"<?php header('X-One: 1'); setcookie('sid', 'abc'); http_response_code(201); echo http_response_code();\"\n45\t       \"201\"\n46\t       :response [{:php.response/header \"X-One: 1\", :replace true}\n47\t                  {:php.response/cookie {:name \"sid\", :value \"abc\"}}\n48\t                  {:php.response/status 201}\n49\t                  {:php.response/body \"201\"}])\n50\t   (fx :headers-after-output\n51\t       \"<?php echo 'x'; header('X-Late: 1'); var_dump(headers_sent());\"\n52\t       \"xbool(true)\\n\"\n53\t       :diag [[2 \"Cannot modify header information - headers already sent\"]]\n54\t       :response [{:php.response/body \"xbool(true)\\n\"}])\n55\t   (fx :error-handler-and-warnings\n56\t       (str \"<?php set_error_handler(function($n, $s) { echo 'H', $n, ':', $s; });\"\n57\t            \" trigger_error('first', E_USER_WARNING); restore_error_handler();\"\n58\t            \" trigger_error('second', E_USER_NOTICE);\")\n59\t       \"H512:first\"\n60\t       :diag [[1024 \"second\"]])\n61\t   (fx :exit-runs-shutdown\n62\t       \"<?php register_shutdown_function(function() { echo 'S'; }); echo 'A'; exit(7); echo 'B';\"\n63\t       \"AS\"\n64\t       :status 7)\n65\t   (fx :exit-string\n66\t       \"<?php echo 'A'; die('B'); echo 'C';\"\n67\t       \"AB\"\n68\t       :status 0)])"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_sdYOgQjLfuiNGN0AfhTjSP6v","content":"1\t(ns yang.php.antlr.builtins\n2\t  \"The pinned PHP builtin catalogue (docs/design/yang.php.md section 3.8): the\n3\t   lower-cased names of the PHP 8.3 core functions a program is likely to\n4\t   call. A call to a name in this set that is neither declared by the unit nor\n5\t   supplied by the prelude gets the `:yang.php/unknown-builtin` warning\n6\t   diagnostic at lowering, so an unsupported library function fails honestly\n7\t   before the program runs. At run time such a call is still\n8\t   `Error: Call to undefined function`; nothing is stubbed to return\n9\t   success. The list is checked in, not derived: regenerate it from\n10\t   `get_defined_functions()['internal']` of the pinned PHP when the target\n11\t   version moves.\")\n12\t\n13\t\n14\t(def supported\n15\t  \"The builtins the prelude supplies: lower-cased PHP name to the prelude\n16\t   definition that implements it and, for a by-reference builtin, the\n17\t   by-reference argument positions (`:by-ref`). The prelude derives its\n18\t   registration from this table and the lowering reads `:by-ref`, so a\n19\t   position is stated once. A by-reference builtin answers `[ret outs]`.\"\n20\t  (let [plain (fn [m] (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k {:prelude v}])) m))\n21\t        by-ref (fn [m] (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k {:prelude v, :by-ref [0]}])) m))]\n22\t    (merge\n23\t      (plain {\"var_dump\" 'php/bi-var-dump, \"intdiv\" 'php/bi-intdiv, \"fmod\" 'php/bi-fmod,\n24\t              \"strlen\" 'php/bi-strlen, \"intval\" 'php/bi-intval, \"floatval\" 'php/bi-floatval,\n25\t              \"strval\" 'php/bi-strval, \"boolval\" 'php/bi-boolval, \"is_nan\" 'php/bi-is-nan,\n26\t              \"set_error_handler\" 'php/bi-set-error-handler,\n27\t              \"restore_error_handler\" 'php/bi-restore-error-handler,\n28\t              \"error_reporting\" 'php/bi-error-reporting,\n29\t              \"trigger_error\" 'php/bi-trigger-error, \"user_error\" 'php/bi-trigger-error,\n30\t              \"ob_start\" 'php/bi-ob-start, \"ob_get_contents\" 'php/bi-ob-get-contents,\n31\t              \"ob_get_clean\" 'php/bi-ob-get-clean, \"ob_end_clean\" 'php/bi-ob-end-clean,\n32\t              \"ob_end_flush\" 'php/bi-ob-end-flush,\n33\t              \"header\" 'php/bi-header, \"headers_sent\" 'php/bi-headers-sent,\n34\t              \"http_response_code\" 'php/bi-http-response-code,\n35\t              \"setcookie\" 'php/bi-setcookie, \"setrawcookie\" 'php/bi-setrawcookie,\n36\t              \"php_sapi_name\" 'php/php-sapi-name, \"getenv\" 'php/bi-getenv,\n37\t              \"count\" 'php/bi-count, \"sizeof\" 'php/bi-count,\n38\t              \"array_keys\" 'php/bi-array-keys, \"array_values\" 'php/bi-array-values,\n39\t              \"array_merge\" 'php/bi-array-merge,\n40\t              \"current\" 'php/bi-current, \"pos\" 'php/bi-current, \"key\" 'php/bi-key,\n41\t              \"implode\" 'php/bi-implode, \"join\" 'php/bi-implode, \"array_sum\" 'php/bi-array-sum,\n42\t              \"array_key_exists\" 'php/bi-array-key-exists,\n43\t              \"key_exists\" 'php/bi-array-key-exists, \"in_array\" 'php/bi-in-array,\n44\t              \"is_array\" 'php/bi-is-array, \"array_key_first\" 'php/bi-array-key-first,\n45\t              \"array_key_last\" 'php/bi-array-key-last, \"get_class\" 'php/bi-get-class,\n46\t              \"register_shutdown_function\" 'php/bi-register-shutdown-function,\n47\t              \"define\" 'php/bi-define, \"defined\" 'php/bi-defined, \"constant\" 'php/bi-constant,\n48\t              \"function_exists\" 'php/bi-function-exists, \"class_exists\" 'php/bi-class-exists,\n49\t              \"spl_autoload_register\" 'php/bi-spl-autoload-register,\n50\t              \"spl_autoload_unregister\" 'php/bi-spl-autoload-unregister,\n51\t              \"spl_autoload_functions\" 'php/bi-spl-autoload-functions,\n52\t              \"spl_autoload_call\" 'php/bi-spl-autoload-call,\n53\t              \"set_exception_handler\" 'php/bi-set-exception-handler,\n54\t              \"restore_exception_handler\" 'php/bi-restore-exception-handler})\n55\t      (by-ref {\"next\" 'php/bi-next, \"prev\" 'php/bi-prev, \"reset\" 'php/bi-reset, \"end\" 'php/bi-end,\n56\t               \"array_push\" 'php/bi-array-push, \"array_pop\" 'php/bi-array-pop,\n57\t               \"array_shift\" 'php/bi-array-shift, \"array_unshift\" 'php/bi-array-unshift,\n58\t               \"sort\" 'php/bi-sort, \"rsort\" 'php/bi-rsort, \"asort\" 'php/bi-asort,\n59\t               \"arsort\" 'php/bi-arsort, \"ksort\" 'php/bi-ksort, \"krsort\" 'php/bi-krsort,\n60\t               \"usort\" 'php/bi-usort, \"uasort\" 'php/bi-uasort, \"uksort\" 'php/bi-uksort}))))\n61\t\n62\t\n63\t(def catalogue\n64\t  #{;; strings\n65\t    \"addslashes\" \"bin2hex\" \"chr\" \"chunk_split\" \"count_chars\" \"crc32\" \"explode\"\n66\t    \"html_entity_decode\" \"htmlentities\" \"htmlspecialchars\" \"implode\" \"join\"\n67\t    \"lcfirst\" \"levenshtein\" \"ltrim\" \"md5\" \"nl2br\" \"number_format\" \"ord\"\n68\t    \"printf\" \"rtrim\" \"sha1\" \"similar_text\" \"sprintf\" \"str_contains\"\n69\t    \"str_ends_with\" \"str_pad\" \"str_repeat\" \"str_replace\" \"str_split\"\n70\t    \"str_starts_with\" \"str_word_count\" \"strcasecmp\" \"strcmp\" \"strip_tags\"\n71\t    \"stripos\" \"stripslashes\" \"stristr\" \"strnatcmp\" \"strncasecmp\" \"strncmp\"\n72\t    \"strpos\" \"strrchr\" \"strrev\" \"strripos\" \"strrpos\" \"strstr\" \"strtolower\"\n73\t    \"strtoupper\" \"strtr\" \"substr\" \"substr_count\" \"substr_replace\" \"trim\"\n74\t    \"ucfirst\" \"ucwords\" \"vsprintf\" \"wordwrap\"\n75\t    ;; multibyte\n76\t    \"mb_strlen\" \"mb_substr\" \"mb_strtolower\" \"mb_strtoupper\" \"mb_strpos\"\n77\t    \"mb_str_split\" \"mb_internal_encoding\" \"mb_strwidth\"\n78\t    ;; arrays\n79\t    \"array_chunk\" \"array_column\" \"array_combine\" \"array_count_values\"\n80\t    \"array_diff\" \"array_diff_key\" \"array_fill\" \"array_fill_keys\" \"array_filter\"\n81\t    \"array_flip\" \"array_intersect\" \"array_intersect_key\" \"array_is_list\"\n82\t    \"array_key_exists\" \"array_key_first\" \"array_key_last\" \"array_keys\"\n83\t    \"array_map\" \"array_merge\" \"array_merge_recursive\" \"array_multisort\"\n84\t    \"array_pad\" \"array_pop\" \"array_product\" \"array_push\" \"array_rand\"\n85\t    \"array_reduce\" \"array_replace\" \"array_reverse\" \"array_search\" \"array_shift\"\n86\t    \"array_slice\" \"array_splice\" \"array_sum\" \"array_unique\" \"array_unshift\"\n87\t    \"array_values\" \"array_walk\" \"arsort\" \"asort\" \"compact\" \"count\" \"current\"\n88\t    \"end\" \"extract\" \"in_array\" \"key\" \"krsort\" \"ksort\" \"list\" \"natsort\" \"next\"\n89\t    \"prev\" \"range\" \"reset\" \"rsort\" \"shuffle\" \"sizeof\" \"sort\" \"uasort\" \"uksort\"\n90\t    \"usort\"\n91\t    ;; math\n92\t    \"abs\" \"acos\" \"asin\" \"atan\" \"atan2\" \"base_convert\" \"bindec\" \"ceil\" \"cos\"\n93\t    \"decbin\" \"dechex\" \"decoct\" \"deg2rad\" \"exp\" \"floor\" \"hexdec\" \"hypot\"\n94\t    \"is_finite\" \"is_infinite\" \"log\" \"log10\" \"log2\" \"max\" \"min\" \"mt_getrandmax\"\n95\t    \"mt_rand\" \"mt_srand\" \"octdec\" \"pi\" \"pow\" \"rad2deg\" \"rand\" \"random_int\"\n96\t    \"round\" \"sin\" \"sqrt\" \"srand\" \"tan\"\n97\t    ;; variables and types\n98\t    \"boolval\" \"empty\" \"floatval\" \"gettype\" \"get_debug_type\" \"intval\" \"is_array\"\n99\t    \"is_bool\" \"is_callable\" \"is_countable\" \"is_float\" \"is_int\" \"is_integer\"\n100\t    \"is_iterable\" \"is_null\" \"is_numeric\" \"is_object\" \"is_scalar\" \"is_string\"\n101\t    \"isset\" \"print_r\" \"serialize\" \"settype\" \"strval\" \"unserialize\" \"unset\"\n102\t    \"var_export\" \"json_encode\" \"json_decode\"\n103\t    ;; functions and classes\n104\t    \"call_user_func\" \"call_user_func_array\" \"class_exists\" \"func_get_arg\"\n105\t    \"func_get_args\" \"func_num_args\" \"function_exists\" \"get_class\"\n106\t    \"get_object_vars\" \"method_exists\" \"property_exists\" \"spl_autoload_register\"\n107\t    \"spl_object_id\" \"iterator_to_array\"\n108\t    ;; output, errors, runtime\n109\t    \"assert\" \"debug_zval_refcount\" \"error_log\" \"flush\" \"ini_get\" \"ini_set\"\n110\t    \"ob_end_clean\" \"ob_end_flush\" \"ob_get_clean\" \"ob_get_contents\" \"ob_start\"\n111\t    \"set_exception_handler\" \"trigger_error\" \"user_error\" \"usleep\" \"sleep\"\n112\t    \"memory_get_usage\" \"microtime\" \"time\" \"date\" \"mktime\" \"strtotime\"\n113\t    \"date_default_timezone_set\" \"hrtime\" \"uniqid\" \"define\" \"defined\"\n114\t    \"constant\" \"php_sapi_name\" \"phpversion\" \"getenv\" \"gc_collect_cycles\"\n115\t    \"file_get_contents\" \"file_put_contents\" \"fopen\" \"fclose\" \"fwrite\" \"fgets\"\n116\t    \"file_exists\" \"preg_match\" \"preg_match_all\" \"preg_replace\" \"preg_split\"\n117\t    \"preg_quote\" \"preg_replace_callback\"})\n118\t\n119\t\n120\t(def constants\n121\t  \"The builtin constants (plan P6 R7), name to value, read by the lowering\n122\t   (a fold in the global block and at fully qualified reads) and by\n123\t   `php/init!` (seeding `php.rt/constants`, so `defined` and `constant`\n124\t   agree with the folded literals). A plain value is its own literal; the\n125\t   vector forms stand for the values a literal cannot express:\n126\t   `[:int text]` an integer past the reader's range, `:nan`, `:inf`,\n127\t   `[:float text value]`.\"\n128\t  (merge\n129\t    {\"PHP_INT_MAX\" [:int \"9223372036854775807\"],\n130\t     \"PHP_INT_MIN\" [:int \"-9223372036854775808\"],\n131\t     \"PHP_INT_SIZE\" 8,\n132\t     \"PHP_EOL\" \"\\n\",\n133\t     \"NAN\" :nan,\n134\t     \"INF\" :inf,\n135\t     \"M_PI\" [:float \"3.141592653589793\" 3.141592653589793]}\n136\t    (zipmap [\"SORT_REGULAR\" \"SORT_NUMERIC\" \"SORT_STRING\" \"SORT_FLAG_CASE\" \"SORT_NATURAL\"\n137\t             \"COUNT_NORMAL\" \"COUNT_RECURSIVE\" \"E_ERROR\" \"E_WARNING\" \"E_PARSE\" \"E_NOTICE\"\n138\t             \"E_CORE_ERROR\" \"E_CORE_WARNING\" \"E_COMPILE_ERROR\" \"E_COMPILE_WARNING\"\n139\t             \"E_USER_ERROR\" \"E_USER_WARNING\" \"E_USER_NOTICE\" \"E_STRICT\"\n140\t             \"E_RECOVERABLE_ERROR\" \"E_DEPRECATED\" \"E_USER_DEPRECATED\" \"E_ALL\"]\n141\t            [0 1 2 8 6 0 1 1 2 4 8 16 32 64 128 256 512 1024 2048 4096 8192 16384 32767])))"}
{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_nhoN9GE7Xry2SYIVk4RM5frE","function":{"name":"Glob","arguments":"{\"pattern\":\"src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/*.cljc\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_NDMXRN7btLN4RroIFNeJQSYM","function":{"name":"Glob","arguments":"{\"pattern\":\"test/yang/php/antlr/*test*.clj*\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_4pLpX7hsnDMrqu9TEmnHfFqA","function":{"name":"Grep","arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/cljc/yang/php/antlr\",\"pattern\":\"bi-array|bi-strlen|dict-scope|local-get|dynamic|eval|VariableVariable|GLOBALS|string offset writes\",\"output_mode\":\"files_with_matches\",\"head_limit\":100}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_QEmmlfQHGGgGnVFatsGRpLC3","function":{"name":"Grep","arguments":"{\"path\":\"test/yang/php/antlr\",\"pattern\":\"programs-p5|request-context|bundled|run-fixture\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"-C\":3,\"head_limit\":150}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_WzLU5T1nLnhcp00aFiNno4iA","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"test/README.md\",\"n_lines\":250}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_WzLU5T1nLnhcp00aFiNno4iA","content":"1\t## ClojureDart Test Suite\n2\t\n3\tClojureDart tests are cross-compiled to Dart and executed using the Dart VM.\n4\t\n5\t### Running ClojureDart Tests\n6\t```bash\n7\tclj -M:clojuredart:cljd test            # all namespaces (sweeps the classpath)\n8\tclj -M:clojuredart:cljd test some.ns    # a subset\n9\t```\n10\tThe native `cljd.build` test command compiles every `.cljc`/`.cljd` namespace on the classpath, generates a `*_test.dart` entrypoint under `test/cljd-out/` for each namespace containing deftests, and runs them via `flutter test`. There is no allowlist: JVM-only namespaces are excluded at the reader level with `#?(:cljd nil :clj ...)` guards (a plain `#?(:clj ...)` does NOT exclude code from the ClojureDart build, because the host pass also matches `:clj`).\n11\t\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t## ClojureScript Test Suite\n15\t\n16\tClojureScript tests are cross-compiled to JavaScript and executed using Node.js.\n17\t\n18\t### Running ClojureScript Tests\n19\t```bash\n20\t./bin/run-cljs-tests.sh\n21\t```\n22\tThis script uses `shadow-cljs` to compile the `:test` build and runs the resulting script with `node`.\n23\t\n24\t### Supported Test Build\n25\tThe configuration for the test build is defined in `shadow-cljs.edn` under the `:test` key.\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## Yin VM Formal Test Suite\n30\t\n31\t## Overview\n32\t\n33\tFormal test suite using `clojure.test` for the Yin Virtual Machine implementation.\n34\t\n35\t## Test Files\n36\t\n37\t### [yin/vm_basic_test.clj](yin/vm_basic_test.clj)\n38\tCore functionality tests covering:\n39\t- ✅ **Literal evaluation** - Numbers and strings\n40\t- ✅ **Variable lookup** - Environment binding\n41\t- ✅ **Lambda/Closure creation** - Captures environment\n42\t- ✅ **Primitive addition** - Direct function application\n43\t- ✅ **Lambda addition** - User-defined functions\n44\t- ✅ **Increment with continuations** - Step-by-step execution\n45\t- ✅ **All arithmetic primitives** - `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`\n46\t- ✅ **All comparison operations** - `=`, `<`, `>`\n47\t\n48\t**Stats:** 8 tests, 16 assertions\n49\t\n50\t## Running Tests\n51\t\n52\t### Quick Run\n53\t```bash\n54\t./run_formal_tests.sh\n55\t```\n56\t\n57\t### Manual Run\n58\t```bash\n59\tclj -M:test -e \"(require 'yin.vm-basic-test) (clojure.test/run-tests 'yin.vm-basic-test)\"\n60\t```\n61\t\n62\t### From REPL\n63\t```clojure\n64\t(require 'yin.vm-basic-test)\n65\t(clojure.test/run-tests 'yin.vm-basic-test)\n66\t```\n67\t\n68\t### Run Specific Test\n69\t```clojure\n70\t(require 'yin.vm-basic-test)\n71\t(clojure.test/test-var #'yin.vm-basic-test/test-lambda-addition)\n72\t```\n73\t\n74\t## Test Structure\n75\t\n76\tEach test follows the standard `clojure.test` pattern:\n77\t\n78\t```clojure\n79\t(deftest test-name\n80\t  (testing \"Description\"\n81\t    (let [ast {...}\n82\t          result (walker/run (walker/make-state env) ast)]\n83\t      (is (= expected (:value result))\n84\t          \"Assertion message\"))))\n85\t```\n86\t\n87\t## Test Coverage\n88\t\n89\t### Covered Features\n90\t- ✅ CESK machine state transitions\n91\t- ✅ Literal value evaluation\n92\t- ✅ Variable environment lookup\n93\t- ✅ Closure creation and application\n94\t- ✅ Primitive function application\n95\t- ✅ Lambda function application\n96\t- ✅ Continuation-based evaluation\n97\t- ✅ All arithmetic operations\n98\t- ✅ All comparison operations\n99\t\n100\t### Known Limitations\n101\t- ⚠️ Nested lambda applications (requires continuation improvements)\n102\t- ⚠️ Nested arithmetic expressions within lambda bodies\n103\t- ⚠️ Conditional (if/then/else) - not yet tested\n104\t\n105\t## Configuration\n106\t\n107\tTests use the `:test` alias from `deps.edn`:\n108\t\n109\t```clojure\n110\t:test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n111\t       :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n112\t                    {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}}}\n113\t```\n114\t\n115\t## Test Output\n116\t\n117\tSuccessful run shows:\n118\t```\n119\tTesting yin.vm-basic-test\n120\t\n121\tRan 8 tests containing 16 assertions.\n122\t0 failures, 0 errors.\n123\t```\n124\t\n125\t## Integration with CI/CD\n126\t\n127\tThese tests can be integrated into CI/CD pipelines:\n128\t\n129\t```bash\n130\t# Exit with error code on test failure\n131\tclj -M:test -e \"(require 'yin.vm-basic-test) (let [result (clojure.test/run-tests 'yin.vm-basic-test)] (System/exit (if (clojure.test/successful? result) 0 1)))\"\n132\t```\n133\t\n134\t## Adding New Tests\n135\t\n136\t1. Create test file in `test/yin/`\n137\t2. Use namespace: `(ns yin.your-test (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]] [yin.vm :as vm]))`\n138\t3. Add tests using `deftest`, `testing`, and `is`\n139\t4. Run with: `clj -M:test -e \"(require 'yin.your-test) (clojure.test/run-tests 'yin.your-test)\"`\n140\t\n141\t## Related Documentation\n142\t\n143\t- **Implementation:** [src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc](../src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc)\n144\t- **Informal Tests:** [test_add.clj](../test_add.clj), [test_simple_continuation.clj](../test_simple_continuation.clj)\n145\t- **Full Documentation:** [YIN_VM_TESTS.md](../YIN_VM_TESTS.md)"}
