{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_JiB2EBWP2wF2U1uCtaPL84fP","content":"1\t(ns yang.php.antlr.request-context-test\n2\t  \"P5 request records, response records, output buffering and isolation.\"\n3\t  (:require\n4\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n5\t    [yang.php.antlr.e2e-harness :as h]\n6\t    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p5 :as p5]))\n7\t\n8\t\n9\t(defn- diagnostics\n10\t  [r]\n11\t  (mapv (juxt :errno :message) (:php/diag r)))\n12\t\n13\t\n14\t(deftest request-binding-smoke-test\n15\t  (is (= \"1\" (:php/out (h/run-raw \"<?php echo 1;\" {})))))\n16\t\n17\t\n18\t(deftest request-context-fixtures-test\n19\t  (doseq [{:keys [id source request out diag response status]} p5/fixtures]\n20\t    (testing (name id)\n21\t      (let [r (h/run-raw source request)]\n22\t        (is (= out (:php/out r)))\n23\t        (is (= (vec diag) (diagnostics r)))\n24\t        (when response (is (= response (:php/response r))))\n25\t        (when status (is (= status (:php/status r))))\n26\t        (is (nil? (:php/uncaught r)))))))\n27\t\n28\t\n29\t(deftest requests-in-separate-tasks-share-nothing-test\n30\t  (let [source (str \"<?php header('X-Request: ' . $_GET['value']);\"\n31\t                    \" echo $_GET['value']; $_GET['value'] = 'changed';\")\n32\t        request-a (assoc p5/request :php.request/query (p5/request-array [[\"value\" \"A\"]]))\n33\t        request-b (assoc p5/request :php.request/query (p5/request-array [[\"value\" \"B\"]]))\n34\t        a (h/run-raw source request-a)\n35\t        b (h/run-raw source request-b)]\n36\t    (is (= \"A\" (:php/out a)))\n37\t    (is (= \"B\" (:php/out b)))\n38\t    (is (= [{:php.response/header \"X-Request: A\", :replace true}\n39\t            {:php.response/body \"A\"}]\n40\t           (:php/response a)))\n41\t    (is (= [{:php.response/header \"X-Request: B\", :replace true}\n42\t            {:php.response/body \"B\"}]\n43\t           (:php/response b)))\n44\t    (is (empty? (:php/diag a)))\n45\t    (is (empty? (:php/diag b)))))"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_X7vgO2ZS1BnCAPqvgIrx21z5","content":"1\t(ns yang.php.antlr.e2e-harness\n2\t  \"The JVM end-to-end harness: PHP source -> CST packet -> lowering stage ->\n3\t   program envelope -> the bundled program on each of the four VMs. Output\n4\t   is the unit's bottom buffer, a latin-1 byte carrier, decoded as UTF-8\n5\t   here at the boundary.\"\n6\t  (:require\n7\t    [clojure.walk :as walk]\n8\t    [dao.host.text :as text]\n9\t    [dao.stream :as stream]\n10\t    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as cst]\n11\t    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n12\t    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as portable]\n13\t    [yang.php.antlr.safepoint :as hooks]\n14\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n15\t    [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\n16\t    [yin.vm :as vm]\n17\t    [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n18\t    [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n19\t    [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n20\t    [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n21\t    [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n22\t    [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n23\t    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n24\t\n25\t\n26\t(defn host-registry\n27\t  \"The registry the PHP compositions run over.\"\n28\t  []\n29\t  (portable/host-registry))\n30\t\n31\t\n32\t(def ^:private base-opts\n33\t  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\n34\t   :capability-secret tu/secret,\n35\t   :primitives vm/primitives})\n36\t\n37\t\n38\t(def ^:private load-semantic\n39\t  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract))\n40\t\n41\t\n42\t(defn lower-program\n43\t  \"`{:ast a :warnings w}` for `source` through the lowering stage, or\n44\t   `{:diagnostics d}`. Warning-severity diagnostics do not stop the program.\"\n45\t  [source]\n46\t  (let [cst-log (tu/new-memory-log)\n47\t        program (tu/new-memory-log)\n48\t        diagnostics (tu/new-memory-log)]\n49\t    (stream/append! cst-log (cst/parse-source source))\n50\t    (lower/step-stage (lower/open-stage cst-log program diagnostics\n51\t                                        {:medium lower/program-medium}))\n52\t    (let [{warnings true, problems false}\n53\t          (group-by #(= :warning (:severity %)) (tu/drain diagnostics))]\n54\t      (if (seq problems)\n55\t        {:diagnostics problems}\n56\t        (let [{:yin/keys [batch root] :as envelope} (first (tu/drain program))]\n57\t          {:ast (nth batch root), :envelope envelope, :warnings (vec warnings)})))))\n58\t\n59\t\n60\t(defn packet->form\n61\t  \"The nested form of a CST packet, spans dropped: `[:rule child ...]` for a\n62\t   rule, `[\\\"TYPE\\\" \\\"text\\\"]` for a token. The inverse of\n63\t   `portable-harness/packet`.\"\n64\t  [{:yang.cst/keys [root nodes]}]\n65\t  (letfn [(form\n66\t            [id]\n67\t            (let [{:keys [kind rule type text children]} (nth nodes id)]\n68\t              (if (= :token kind)\n69\t                [type text]\n70\t                (into [(keyword rule)] (map form) children))))]\n71\t    (form root)))\n72\t\n73\t\n74\t(defn latin1->text\n75\t  \"The UTF-8 text of the byte carrier `s`.\"\n76\t  [s]\n77\t  (text/utf8-decode (.getBytes ^String s \"ISO-8859-1\")))\n78\t\n79\t\n80\t(defn render\n81\t  \"The text a unit prints: its output, then, for an uncaught error, the\n82\t   fatal line (no path, plan section 3.9).\"\n83\t  [{:php/keys [out uncaught fatal]}]\n84\t  (str (latin1->text out)\n85\t       (when uncaught\n86\t         (str \"PHP Fatal error:  Uncaught \" (:class uncaught) \": \" (:message uncaught)))\n87\t       (when fatal\n88\t         (str \"PHP Fatal error:  \" fatal))))\n89\t\n90\t\n91\t(defn run-vms\n92\t  \"`{vm-key rendered}` of `ast` on the four VMs; a host throw is\n93\t   `[:thrown message]`. `:execution-budget` derives the PHP safepoint hooks\n94\t   and starts one per-run counter; no option leaves the AST unchanged.\"\n95\t  ([registry ast] (run-vms registry ast {}))\n96\t  ([registry ast {:keys [execution-budget envelope]}]\n97\t   (let [ast (if (some? execution-budget)\n98\t               (let [projected (encoder/project envelope)\n99\t                     derived (:envelope (safepoint/derive-envelope\n100\t                                          projected hooks/profile :test/derived))\n101\t                     tree (nth (:yin/batch derived) (:yin/root derived))]\n102\t                 (hooks/program execution-budget\n103\t                                (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast tree)))\n104\t               ast)\n105\t         opts (assoc base-opts :modules registry)\n106\t         session (tu/make-observer-session (tu/create-vm {:modules registry}))\n107\t         datoms (vec (vm/ast->datoms ast))\n108\t         projected #(:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))\n109\t         attempt (fn [f]\n110\t                   (try (render (f))\n111\t                        (catch Exception e [:thrown (ex-message e)])))]\n112\t     (tu/queue-ast! session ast)\n113\t     {:ast-walker (attempt #(vm/value (:consumer (tu/run-session session)))),\n114\t      :semantic (attempt #(vm/value (vm/run (load-semantic (semantic/create-vm opts)\n115\t                                                           datoms)))),\n116\t      :stack (attempt #(vm/value (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\n117\t                                           (:image (derive/stack-image (projected)))\n118\t                                           (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))))),\n119\t      :register (attempt #(vm/value (vm/run (rvm/create-vm\n120\t                                              (derive/register-image (projected))\n121\t                                              (assoc opts\n122\t                                                     :contract\n123\t                                                     vm/register-contract)))))})))\n124\t\n125\t\n126\t(defn run-php\n127\t  \"`{vm-key rendered}` for `source`, or `{:diagnostics d}`. The optional\n128\t   `:execution-budget` is a count of PHP `:loop` and `:call` safepoints.\"\n129\t  ([source] (run-php source {}))\n130\t  ([source options]\n131\t   (let [{:keys [ast diagnostics envelope]} (lower-program source)]\n132\t     (if diagnostics\n133\t       {:diagnostics diagnostics}\n134\t       (run-vms (host-registry) ast (assoc options :envelope envelope))))))\n135\t\n136\t\n137\t(defn run-walker\n138\t  \"The ast-walker's rendering of `source` alone (fast iteration).\"\n139\t  [source]\n140\t  (let [{:keys [ast diagnostics]} (lower-program source)]\n141\t    (if diagnostics\n142\t      {:diagnostics diagnostics}\n143\t      (let [registry (host-registry)\n144\t            session (tu/make-observer-session (tu/create-vm {:modules registry}))]\n145\t        (tu/queue-ast! session ast)\n146\t        (try (render (vm/value (:consumer (tu/run-session session))))\n147\t             (catch Exception e [:thrown (ex-message e)]))))))\n148\t\n149\t\n150\t(defn run-raw\n151\t  \"The unit's value on the AST walker, optionally after binding a request record.\"\n152\t  ([source] (run-raw source nil))\n153\t  ([source request]\n154\t   (let [{:keys [ast diagnostics]} (lower-program source)]\n155\t     (if diagnostics\n156\t       {:diagnostics diagnostics}\n157\t       (let [session (tu/make-observer-session\n158\t                       (tu/create-vm {:modules (host-registry)}))\n159\t             ast (if request\n160\t                   (walk/postwalk\n161\t                     (fn [node]\n162\t                       (if (and (map? node)\n163\t                                (= :application (:type node))\n164\t                                (= 'php/run-main (get-in node [:operator :name])))\n165\t                         (let [body (first (:operands node))]\n166\t                           (assoc node :operands\n167\t                                  [(u/lam []\n168\t                                          (u/then\n169\t                                            (u/sexp->uast (list 'php/bind-request! request))\n170\t                                            (u/app body)))]))\n171\t                         node))\n172\t                     ast)\n173\t                   ast)]\n174\t         (tu/queue-ast! session ast)\n175\t         (vm/value (:consumer (tu/run-session session))))))))"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_3d09zvrf65RngrRVxIATzRAt","content":"1\t(ns yang.php.antlr.scope\n2\t  \"PHP scope analysis over a CST packet (docs/design/yang.php.md section 7.3).\n3\t\n4\t   A scope is opened by the unit and by each function declaration, keyed by\n5\t   that node's CST id. For each scope:\n6\t\n7\t     :kind            :unit | :function\n8\t     :params          parameter variable names in order, sigil included\n9\t     :assigned        variable names written in the scope, first occurrence\n10\t                      first (parameters and statics included)\n11\t     :vars            every variable name the scope mentions, first occurrence\n12\t                      first (what a function allocates local cells for)\n13\t     :statics         names declared `static`\n14\t     :globals         names declared `global`\n15\t     :uses            closure `use` names (closures are refused in P1)\n16\t     :arrow-captures  arrow-function captures (refused in P1)\n17\t     :dynamic?        true when the scope names a variable dynamically\n18\t                      (`$$x`, `${...}`)\n19\t     :includes?       true when the scope holds an include/require expression\n20\t                      (outside nested functions): the dynamic-scope profile\n21\t                      of plan P6 R5\n22\t     :this?           true when the scope reads `$this`\n23\t\n24\t   P1 consumes `:kind :params :assigned :statics`; the rest are computed here\n25\t   so later slices read them without a second walk. A nested function's body\n26\t   is not scanned for the enclosing scope.\"\n27\t  (:require\n28\t    [yang.antlr.packet :as p]))\n29\t\n30\t\n31\t(def ^:private scope-rules\n32\t  #{\"functionDeclaration\" \"lambdaFunctionExpr\"})\n33\t\n34\t\n35\t(defn- method?\n36\t  \"A class member that is a method: a `classStatement` with `function`.\"\n37\t  [pk k]\n38\t  (and (p/rule? k \"classStatement\")\n39\t       (boolean (some #(and (p/token? %) (= \"Function_\" (:type %))) (p/children pk k)))))\n40\t\n41\t\n42\t(defn- empty-scope\n43\t  [kind]\n44\t  {:kind kind,\n45\t   :params [],\n46\t   :assigned [],\n47\t   :vars [],\n48\t   :statics [],\n49\t   :globals [],\n50\t   :uses [],\n51\t   :arrow-captures [],\n52\t   :dynamic? false,\n53\t   :includes? false,\n54\t   :this? false})\n55\t\n56\t\n57\t(defn- note-name\n58\t  [scope k name]\n59\t  (if (some #{name} (get scope k)) scope (update scope k conj name)))\n60\t\n61\t\n62\t(defn- var-name\n63\t  \"The variable name of a `variableInitializer`, sigil included.\"\n64\t  [pk n]\n65\t  (:text (first (filter #(p/token? %) (p/children pk n)))))\n66\t\n67\t\n68\t(defn- chain-base\n69\t  \"The base variable of `chain`, sigil included: `$a` for `$a`, `$a[0][]`,\n70\t   `$a{1}`; nil when the chain is not a variable with offsets.\"\n71\t  [pk chain]\n72\t  (when (p/rule? chain \"chain\")\n73\t    (let [origin (first (p/children pk chain))\n74\t          base (when (p/rule? origin \"chainOrigin\") (first (p/children pk origin)))\n75\t          keyed (when (p/rule? base \"chainBase\") (first (p/children pk base)))\n76\t          [v & offsets] (when (p/rule? keyed \"keyedVariable\") (p/children pk keyed))]\n77\t      (when (and v\n78\t                 (p/token? v)\n79\t                 (= \"VarName\" (:type v))\n80\t                 (every? #(p/rule? % \"squareCurlyExpression\") offsets))\n81\t        (:text v)))))\n82\t\n83\t\n84\t(defn- assign-targets\n85\t  \"Variable names an assignment expression writes: the base variable of its\n86\t   `assignable` chain (`$a[k] = v` writes `$a`).\"\n87\t  [pk n]\n88\t  (let [target (first (p/children pk n))]\n89\t    (when (p/rule? target \"assignable\")\n90\t      (some-> (chain-base pk (first (p/children pk target))) vector))))\n91\t\n92\t\n93\t(defn- foreach-targets\n94\t  \"Base variables a `foreach` writes: the value target and the key target.\"\n95\t  [pk n]\n96\t  (let [kids (p/children pk n)\n97\t        after-arrow (rest (drop-while #(not (p/token? % \"=>\")) kids))]\n98\t    (keep identity\n99\t          (concat (map #(chain-base pk (first (p/children pk %)))\n100\t                       (filter #(p/rule? % \"assignable\") kids))\n101\t                  (map #(chain-base pk %) (filter #(p/rule? % \"chain\") after-arrow))))))\n102\t\n103\t\n104\t(defn- include-expr?\n105\t  \"True for `include`/`include_once`/`require`/`require_once <operand>`.\"\n106\t  [pk n]\n107\t  (let [kids (p/children pk n)]\n108\t    (and (= 2 (count kids))\n109\t         (p/token? (first kids))\n110\t         (contains? #{\"Include\" \"IncludeOnce\" \"Require\" \"RequireOnce\"} (:type (first kids))))))\n111\t\n112\t\n113\t(declare analyze-fn)\n114\t\n115\t\n116\t(defn- fold-closure\n117\t  \"The enclosing `scope` plus what a closure takes from it: the `use`\n118\t   variables (assigned when by reference), or, for an arrow function, every\n119\t   variable its body mentions that is not its own parameter.\"\n120\t  [pk k inner scope]\n121\t  (if (some #(and (p/token? %) (= \"LambdaFn\" (:type %))) (p/children pk k))\n122\t    (reduce #(note-name %1 :vars %2)\n123\t            scope\n124\t            (remove (set (:params inner)) (:vars inner)))\n125\t    (reduce (fn [sc uv]\n126\t              (let [kids (p/children pk uv)\n127\t                    nm (:text (last kids))\n128\t                    sc (note-name sc :vars nm)]\n129\t                (if (some #(p/token? % \"&\") kids) (note-name sc :assigned nm) sc)))\n130\t            scope\n131\t            (mapcat #(p/child-rules pk % \"lambdaFunctionUseVar\")\n132\t                    (p/child-rules pk k \"lambdaFunctionUseVars\")))))\n133\t\n134\t\n135\t(defn- walk\n136\t  \"Add the bindings below `n` to `scope`; a nested scope-opening rule is\n137\t   recorded in `scopes` and not walked into.\"\n138\t  [pk n [scope scopes]]\n139\t  (reduce\n140\t    (fn [[scope scopes :as acc] k]\n141\t      (cond\n142\t        (not (p/rule? k)) (if (= \"VarName\" (:type k))\n143\t                            [(note-name scope :vars (:text k)) scopes]\n144\t                            acc)\n145\t        (or (contains? scope-rules (:rule k)) (method? pk k))\n146\t        (let [[s ss] (analyze-fn pk k scopes)]\n147\t          [(if (= \"lambdaFunctionExpr\" (:rule k))\n148\t             (fold-closure pk k s scope)\n149\t             scope)\n150\t           (assoc ss (:id k) s)])\n151\t        :else\n152\t        (let [scope (case (:rule k)\n153\t                      \"staticVariableStatement\"\n154\t                      (reduce (fn [sc v]\n155\t                                (let [nm (var-name pk v)]\n156\t                                  (-> sc\n157\t                                      (note-name :statics nm)\n158\t                                      (note-name :assigned nm))))\n159\t                              scope\n160\t                              (p/child-rules pk k \"staticInitializer\"))\n161\t                      \"globalStatement\"\n162\t                      (reduce (fn [sc v]\n163\t                                (if (p/token? v)\n164\t                                  (if (= \"VarName\" (:type v))\n165\t                                    (note-name sc :globals (:text v))\n166\t                                    sc)\n167\t                                  sc))\n168\t                              scope\n169\t                              (mapcat #(p/children pk %)\n170\t                                      (p/child-rules pk k \"globalVar\")))\n171\t                      \"expression\"\n172\t                      (cond-> (reduce #(note-name %1 :assigned %2)\n173\t                                      scope\n174\t                                      (assign-targets pk k))\n175\t                        (include-expr? pk k) (assoc :includes? true))\n176\t                      \"foreachStatement\"\n177\t                      (reduce #(note-name %1 :assigned %2)\n178\t                              scope\n179\t                              (foreach-targets pk k))\n180\t                      scope)\n181\t              scope (if (and (p/rule? k \"keyedVariable\")\n182\t                             (some #(p/token? % \"$\") (p/children pk k)))\n183\t                      (assoc scope :dynamic? true)\n184\t                      scope)\n185\t              scope (if (some #(p/token? % \"$this\") (p/children pk k))\n186\t                      (assoc scope :this? true)\n187\t                      scope)]\n188\t          (walk pk k [scope scopes]))))\n189\t    [scope scopes]\n190\t    (p/children pk n)))\n191\t\n192\t\n193\t(defn- analyze-fn\n194\t  [pk fn-node scopes]\n195\t  (let [params (->> (p/child-rules pk fn-node \"formalParameterList\")\n196\t                    (mapcat #(p/child-rules pk % \"formalParameter\"))\n197\t                    (keep (fn [fp]\n198\t                            (some->> (p/child-rules pk fp \"variableInitializer\")\n199\t                                     first\n200\t                                     (var-name pk)))))\n201\t        base (reduce #(note-name (note-name %1 :assigned %2) :vars %2)\n202\t                     (assoc (empty-scope :function) :params (vec params))\n203\t                     params)]\n204\t    (walk pk fn-node [base scopes])))\n205\t\n206\t\n207\t(defn analyze\n208\t  \"The analysis of packet `pk`: `{:unit scope, :scopes {fn-node-id scope}}`.\"\n209\t  [pk]\n210\t  (let [[unit scopes] (walk pk (p/root pk) [(empty-scope :unit) {}])]\n211\t    {:unit unit, :scopes scopes}))"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_cQLkUOcl1tqYhRbJUFC0oSTp","content":"src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-33-   `php.rt/state` (the literal `:php/uninit` until `php/init!` flips it to\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-34-   `:php/ready` as its last write):\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:35:     php.rt/ctx            the dynamic context {:handlers :depth :base :frame}\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-36-     php.rt/out            a cell holding the buffer stack, a vector of\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-37-                           buffers, each a vector of byte-string chunks;\n--\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-39-                           bottom buffer is never popped\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-40-     php.rt/globals        a cell holding the plain array of section 10.1\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:41:                           (`$GLOBALS`), `(php/empty-array)` initially\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-42-     php.rt/functions      a cell holding a map of lower-cased name to\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-43-                           function cell; builtins are pre-seeded\n--\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-160-\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-161-    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- escapes\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:162:    ;; The dynamic context is one record in one cell: every capture point\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-163-    ;; saves it and every escape restores it with :base left alone. The\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-164-    ;; handler stack is a chain of frames [kind payload rest n depth].\n--\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-2058-\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-2059-    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- variables\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2060:    ;; Top-level variables live in `php.rt/globals` (the `$GLOBALS` array\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc-