{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_mDrCZuxHVz8ccaTtfo1xMfMF","content":"docs/design/yang.antlr.md-28-implementation or conformance claim: the Python, TypeScript, and PHP\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-29-preludes still have different callable entry paths. The related amendments\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-30-in sections 8.1, 8.5.6, and 8.11 have the same status.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-31-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-32-Updated 2026-10-01 with the Architect rulings of 2026-09-30 and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-33-2026-10-01, each accepted by the owner. Later sections cite them by the\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-34-short names given here:\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-35-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-36-- the cell ruling; mob D1 to D10 (round 2); the mutable-objects ruling;\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-37-  the Python mappability ruling.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-38-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-39-They amend sections 8.1, 8.5, 9.3, 9.4, and 9.5, add sections 8.5.1 and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:40:8.11, and add cross-references from sections 8.6 and 8.9. Landed on\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-41-master since: captured continuations are invocable on all four VMs\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-42-(`8f9f90b0`); effects are an unforgeable host type and callee profiles\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-43-bound the effects they may raise (mob D4, `9a69e58f`); task-heap cells,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-44-slice 1 (`5e790683`); and the pure `data` host module (`yin.vm.data`,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-45-`fe8bce4a`).\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-46-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-47-Updated 2026-10-02 with three further ruling sets, cited by these short\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-48-names:\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-49-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-50-- the safepoint design, whose seven owner decisions the owner accepted\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-51-  on 2026-10-01 (\"accept all recommendations\");\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-52-- the C2 generator design and the C2 cross-ruling;\n--\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-155-Validation and publication interpreter ----> Reference and provenance\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-156-  |                                          ledger\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-157-  v\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-158-Admitted program row stream --------------> Independent AST indexer\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-159-  |                    |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-160-  |                    v\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-161-  |            Optional macro expansion stage\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-162-  |                    |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-163-  v                    v\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-164-Evaluator observer <---+\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-165-```\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-166-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:167:The direct evaluator route and the macro route are composition\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:168:alternatives. A composition must not feed both into one evaluator and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-169-execute the program twice.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-170-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-171-Every substantial stage communicates through a supplied stream. Pure\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-172-helper functions inside a stage may share algorithms; they do not become\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-173-a hidden route between stages or across hosts.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-174-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-175-Diagnostics and lifecycle records use separate supplied streams or\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-176-explicitly framed topics. `dao.stream` does not route records by language\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-177-or payload type.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-178-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-179----\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-180-\n--\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-249-- **No hidden global state:** frontend catalogs, installed\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-250-  implementations, configuration, allocation counters, and caches belong\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-251-  to an explicit composition or worker.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-252-- **No implicit control flow:** admission, parse completion, retries,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-253-  cancellation, publication, and execution are represented by state\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-254-  transitions and stream records.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-255-- **No application callbacks:** host events are classified into data and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-256-  deposited. Portable interpreters poll their own cursors.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-257-- **No shared mutable state:** compiler state is immutable and threaded\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-258-  explicitly. ANTLR's mutable machinery is confined to an exclusively\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-259-  owned host worker.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-260-- **No collapse of interpretation and execution:** streams do not parse,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:261:  compile, schedule, or evaluate; compilation does not execute the\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-262-  user's program.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-263-- **No assumed graphs:** CST child edges, module dependencies, object\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-264-  references, and code relationships are explicit data. Interpreters\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-265-  construct the corresponding relations.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-266-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-267----\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-268-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-269-## 3. Language frontend SPI\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-270-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-271-### 3.1 Portable declarations versus installed implementations\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-272-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-273-A frontend consists of four independently versioned parts:\n--\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-442-### 3.6 Adding a language without core changes\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-443-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-444-A third-party author must be able to:\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-445-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-446-1. Package a grammar and audited dependencies.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-447-2. Declare entry rules, dialect options, and syntax export profile.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-448-3. Supply a lowering and runtime profile.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-449-4. Pass the frontend conformance kit.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-450-5. Add the package to a composition's catalog.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-451-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-452-This changes deployment configuration and adds a plugin package. It does\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-453-not add a language-specific branch to Yang core, DaoStream, the canonical\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:454:AST grammar, or evaluator dispatch.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-455-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-456-Clojure should implement the same frontend contract through its existing\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-457-reader. The open SPI should not require every frontend to use ANTLR.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-458-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-459-### 3.7 Versioning\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-460-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-461-Four things are versioned independently and pinned together per request:\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-462-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-463-- The SPI revision (`:yang.frontend/spi`).\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-464-- The frontend package revision (`:yang.frontend/revision`), which is\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-465-  immutable once published.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-466-- The grammar package content address and its export profile.\n--\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-856-Handles stay in host-local composition. Portable state carries\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-857-identities and descriptors where needed; it does not serialize handles.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-858-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-859-Budgets cover reads, transitions, writes, and work on large structures.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-860-Existing synchronous encoding, hashing, validation, or query helpers\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-861-must be made stepped or run in workers when their input can be large.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-862-Adding a `budget` argument around an unbounded recursive function is\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-863-insufficient.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-864-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-865-The caller drives steps. Cadence or `dao.stream.waitset` can reduce idle\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-866-polling, but no interpreter requires a readiness extension.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-867-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:868:A compilation request is itself an effect descriptor appended by\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-869-portable code: it names the source unit revision, the frontend revision\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-870-and dialect, and the options, and it carries a request identity. The\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-871-compiler coordinator consumes those descriptors and appends outcomes.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-872-Portable code never calls the compiler as a function.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-873-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-874-### 6.2 Respect the existing outcome algebra\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-875-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-876-Compiler outcomes and DaoStream outcomes occupy different layers:\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-877-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-878-```clojure\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-879-;; Successful observation of a failed compilation.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-880-{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n--\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1143-  reference value `{:type :cell-ref :id :cell-N :seal s}` into a\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1144-  task-scoped `:heap` field of the VM value, reached through the `cell`\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1145-  host module: `cell/new`, `cell/get`, and `cell/set!`. A write yields a\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1146-  new VM value; nothing host-mutable is introduced. No AST tag is added,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1147-  and `yin/def`, Rule R, `:vm/store-put`, and the canonical grammar are\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1148-  unchanged.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1149-- Cells have box semantics: they are shared across continuation\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1150-  re-entries and never rolled back, so mutations made before a `raise`\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1151-  persist at the handler.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1152-- Explicit state threading stays an allowed per-frontend choice. Either\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1153-  lowering can be implemented by a stream-consuming interpreter.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1154-- References are logical identities: a `:cell-ref` is data, and a forged\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1155:  or foreign ref fails closed at the evaluator.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1156-- Loops lower to recursive lambdas. Continuations are used for the\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1157-  escapes (`break`, `continue`, `return`), because a continuation takes\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1158-  exactly one argument.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1159-- Abrupt completion (return, throw, break, continue, yield) lowers to\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1160-  captured continuations, not explicit completion records (cell ruling,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1161-  owner decision 5). Locals assigned inside `try` bodies and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1162-  continuation-exited loops therefore need cells.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1163-- Suspended state consists of portable code references and data.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1164-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1165-In this document a \"store cell\" or \"binding cell\" means a `cell` module\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1166-ref over the task heap. It is not a location in the named store: the\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1167-named store stays statically keyed under Rule R and holds `yin/def`\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1168-definitions.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1169-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1170-Every function-local binding and every parameter is a cell, allocated at\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1171-function entry with an unbound sentinel (mob D5). A continuation\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1172-captures its environment, so an env-bound local assigned between capture\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1173-and invocation would rewind; a closure that refers to a name before its\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1174-first assignment needs a pre-established location. Binding collection\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1175-(which names are local to a function, and where `global` and `nonlocal`\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1176-apply) is part of the required lowering stage. Liveness analysis and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1177-un-boxing are a separately attached interpreter that reads the naive\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1178-lowering's stream and writes its own; the composition chooses which\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1179:stream the evaluator reads, and correctness never depends on an optional\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1180-observer.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1181-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1182-Cells cross task boundaries by copy (mob D1). Aliases and cycles are\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1183-preserved within one transferred value graph, and the receiver mints\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1184-fresh ids and re-seals. Cell slice 1 refuses every cell-bearing lift.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1185-There is no cross-task shared cell; cross-task shared state requires an\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1186-explicit stream protocol.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1187-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1188-Aliased guest objects share logical identity, not host mutable objects.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1189-Concurrent access to a guest heap has one owning interpreter or an\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1190-explicitly defined stream protocol. Section 8.11 states how mutable guest\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1191-objects and collections are represented over cells.\nResults truncated to 180 lines (total: 1140). Use offset=180 to see more."}
