{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_rLDyfsBvg8yKvZIRUCkKFOYH","content":"src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-2-  \"The local Yin shell for DaoStream: explicit state, synchronous steps.\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-3-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-4-   This namespace owns no socket, atom, promise, callback, clock, or namespace\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:5:   global.  It holds the one shell value a driver threads: the evaluator beside\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-6-   its separately-owned program media — `program-in`, which the macro\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:7:   expander observes, and `program-out`, which the evaluator's own observer\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-8-   watches (`docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md` §10.1) — the language, the value\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-9-   history, the output medium with its cursor, and a per-medium ledger\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-10-   recording the last outcome that medium answered.  Every function takes a\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-50-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-51-(def ingress-capacity\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-52-  \"Declared capacity of the composition-owned program medium, in elements.  The\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:53:   shell is the only appender and its one step owner serializes evaluation, so\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-54-   eviction can only follow a producer the composition does not make; a gap is\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:55:   therefore fatal to the current evaluation rather than a normal operating\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-56-   condition.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-57-  4096)\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-58-\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-73-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-74-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-75-(def link-round-budget\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:76:  \"How many serve-and-run rounds one evaluation drives while its VM waits\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-77-   on a link (yin.vm.linker.md sections 6.3 and 7.2).  A round serves the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-78-   interpreter once and runs the VM once; a local content source answers\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-79-   within a few, so the budget is reached only by a link that stays\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-120-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-121-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-122-(def query-drive-budget\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:123:  \"The most `dao.space.query/q` calls one drive answers: one evaluation,\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-124-   or one re-check of a pending run.  A query is answered in the round\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-125-   it is asked, so without a bound a program that calls `q` without end\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-126-   would hold its input round in the drive forever.  Each call re-reads\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-131-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-132-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-133-(def query-call-limit-text\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:134:  (str \"the evaluation called dao.space.query/q more than \"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-135-       query-drive-budget\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-136-       \" times and was stopped (:yin.repl.query/call-limit)\"))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-137-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-138-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-139-(def vm-constructors\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:140:  \"The evaluators on `yin.vm`: the ast-walker, the semantic register VM,\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-141-   and the nameless de Bruijn stack and register kernels, each starting with an empty image.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-142-  {:ast-walker ast-walker/create-vm\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-143-   :semantic semantic/create-vm\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-203-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-204-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-205-(def program-loaders\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:206:  \"The loader the evaluator observer hands each `program-out` value, per\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:207:   evaluator.  Every value there is one expanded canonical tree packet\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-208-   `[root rows]` (yin.vm.macro.md §2.4); each loader takes its row set — the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-209-   ast-walker through `vm-load-rows`, the semantic VM through\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-210-   `semantic/load-vector` over the v4 projection, and the de Bruijn\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-211-   kernels through A-derived stack and register images.\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:212:   No evaluator learns that an expander ran.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-213-  {:ast-walker (fn [vm packet]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-214-                 (ast-walker/vm-load-rows vm\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-215-                                          (macro/packet->row-set packet)\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-262-       \"  (repl-state)\\n\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-263-       \"  (help)\\n\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-264-       \"  (quit)\\n\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:265:       \"  *1, *2, *3  - last, second-to-last, and third-to-last evaluated\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-266-       \" values\"))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-267-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-268-\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-287-       \"built (yin.vm.telemetry, opt-in via the :telemetry {:stream ...} \"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-288-       \"construction option — yin.vm.telemetry.implementation-plan.md), but \"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-289-       \"composing a sink into this shell is not, so the command reports \"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:290:       \"rather than evaluates\"))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-291-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-292-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-293-(def ingress-loss-text\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-294-  (str \"One or more program batches were never observed from the program \"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:295:       \"medium; (reset) is required before more evaluation\"))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-296-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-297-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-298-(def result-loss-text\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:299:  \"the evaluation halted but its result never reached the output medium\")\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-300-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-301-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-302-;; =============================================================================\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-478-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-479-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-480-(defn- emit-result!\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:481:  \"Answer a halted evaluation's value on the output medium, after the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-482-   output it printed, so the shell reads results from the stream exactly as\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-483-   it reads prints.  The token carries `round`, so the shell accepts only\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-484-   this round's result.  Returns the append outcome, or `:untried` when\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-620-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-621-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-622-(defn make-vm\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:623:  \"Construct the shell's evaluator on `yin.vm`.\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-624-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-625-   The shell is the composition that chooses the VM's transport: the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:626:   evaluator is handed `:make-stream` bound to the ring buffer and the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-627-   `stream` module registered in its registry.  No telemetry stream is\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-628-   installed, and the VM owns no program medium: `make-session` builds the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-629-   medium, its attachment, the observer, and the VM together.\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-677-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-678-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-679-(defn- make-runner\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:680:  \"The run step the evaluator observer hands each loaded program: run the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-681-   VM through its protocol entry point, as a plain function so it can be\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-682-   handed to observer coordination on every host, and answer a halted\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-683-   run's value on `output-stream` under `round`.  The shell reads the value\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-740-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-741-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-742-(defn- make-session\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:743:  \"Build the evaluator, its media, their attachments and observers, the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:744:   expander, and the loader the evaluator observer feeds the VM, together.\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-745-   Reset and VM selection call this, so the whole composition is rebuilt as\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-746-   one and each attachment capability is bound exactly once per medium\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-747-   lifetime.\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-748-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:749:   Both evaluators sit behind the same two stages (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1):\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-750-   the expander observes `program-in` — `:program-stream`, watched by\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-751-   `:observer` — and appends each expanded tree packet to `program-out` —\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:752:   `:row-stream`, watched independently by the evaluator's `:row-observer`,\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-753-   which loads each packet and runs it.  The code indexer's observer\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-754-   (`yin.repl.index`) is a peer attached to `program-out` beside it; the\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-755-   round advances each, and neither calls the other.  It records\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-863-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-864-   `:index-recovery` carries what the durable open recovered —\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-865-   `{:manifest <address or nil> :datoms <the validated snapshot or nil>}`\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:866:   — and the indexer is rehydrated from it here, before any evaluation\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-867-   is admitted (`yin.repl.index/rehydrate`): `q` answers the previous\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-868-   run's facts, which keep their own session tokens, while this process\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-869-   mints a new token for its own.  In durable mode `(reset)` and `(vm …)`\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1080-\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1081-(defn- commit-frontend\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1082-  \"Keep what a frontend program's lowering staged (`::frontend`, see\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1083:   `eval-compiled`) now that its VM state survives: the frontend session\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1084-   it leaves becomes the shell's `:frontend-session`.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1085-  [state]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1086-  (let [staged (::frontend state)]\n--\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1088-      (contains? staged :session) (assoc :frontend-session (:se