{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_ySqi2oQ120UUu8zIfKt2nMXr","content":"315\t\n316\t(defn issue-ref\n317\t  \"A reference of `kind` (`:stream-ref`, `:cursor-ref`, or `:cell-ref`) to\n318\t   resource or heap cell `id`, sealed under the task's capability secret.\n319\t   A task composed\n320\t   without a secret cannot issue one: it fails closed rather than issue a\n321\t   reference anyone could forge.\"\n322\t  [state kind id]\n323\t  (let [secret (:capability-secret state)]\n324\t    (when (nil? secret)\n325\t      (fail (str \"This task has no capability secret, so it cannot issue\"\n326\t                 \" a resource reference\")\n327\t            {:reason :no-capability-secret, :kind kind, :id id}))\n328\t    {:type kind, :id id, :seal (seal-of secret kind id)}))\n329\t\n330\t\n331\t(defn authentic-ref?\n332\t  \"True when `ref` is a `kind` reference this task issued: its seal\n333\t   verifies under the task's secret, and it names a live resource of that\n334\t   kind. A `:cell-ref` is checked against `:heap` instead: its id is live\n335\t   by `contains?` (a cell may hold nil) and its seal equals the one the\n336\t   heap entry recorded at allocation, so no hash is computed per access.\"\n337\t  [state kind ref]\n338\t  (let [secret (:capability-secret state)\n339\t        id (when (map? ref) (:id ref))]\n340\t    (if (= :cell-ref kind)\n341\t      (let [heap (:heap state)]\n342\t        (boolean (and (some? secret)\n343\t                      (= kind (:type ref))\n344\t                      (contains? heap id)\n345\t                      (= (:seal ref) (:seal (get heap id))))))\n346\t      (let [resource (get (:resources state) id)]\n347\t        (boolean (and (some? secret)\n348\t                      (= kind (:type ref))\n349\t                      (some? resource)\n350\t                      (= (:seal ref) (seal-of secret kind id))\n351\t                      (= (= :cursor-ref kind) (cursor-cell? resource))))))))\n352\t\n353\t\n354\t(defn check-ref!\n355\t  \"The resource id a program-supplied `kind` reference names, once its\n356\t   seal verifies (r10). Anything else fails closed with\n357\t   `:forged-resource-reference`, naming the effect and the id it named;\n358\t   a cell ref whose id the heap does not hold is\n359\t   `:dead-or-forged-reference` instead: its cell was swept, or never was.\n360\t   Ids are never reused, so such a ref is never silently reallocated.\"\n361\t  [state effect-kind kind ref]\n362\t  (if (authentic-ref? state kind ref)\n363\t    (:id ref)\n364\t    (let [id (when (map? ref) (:id ref))\n365\t          dead? (and (= :cell-ref kind) (not (contains? (:heap state) id)))]\n366\t      (fail (if dead? \"Dead or forged cell reference\" \"Forged resource reference\")\n367\t            {:reason (if dead?\n368\t                       :dead-or-forged-reference\n369\t                       :forged-resource-reference),\n370\t             :effect effect-kind,\n371\t             :kind kind,\n372\t             :id id}))))\n373\t\n374\t\n375\t(declare gensym)\n376\t\n377\t\n378\t(defn attach-resource\n379\t  \"Install the host stream `handle` a composition hands a task under a\n380\t   fresh resource id, and return `[stream-ref state]` with the reference\n381\t   sealed under the task's secret. This is how a stream reaches a program:\n382\t   never through the store.\"\n383\t  [state handle]\n384\t  (let [[id state] (gensym state \"stream\")\n385\t        ref (issue-ref state :stream-ref id)]\n386\t    [ref (assoc-in state [:resources id] handle)]))\n387\t\n388\t\n389\t(def ^:private wake-error-outcomes\n390\t  \"The declared outcomes `handle-next` and `handle-put` raise as errors,\n391\t   by wait reason: the read defects for a parked reader, the write defects\n392\t   for a parked writer. A wake raises these exactly as the immediate\n393\t   operation would. Every other status is either a value answer or an\n394\t   outcome outside this contract version, and both of those the immediate\n395\t   path answers as data -- so the wake answers them as data too.\"\n396\t  {:next #{:dao.stream/cursor-mismatch :dao.stream/invalid-cursor\n397\t           :dao.stream/transport-error}\n398\t   :put #{:dao.stream/closed :dao.stream/invalid-value\n399\t          :dao.stream/transport-error}})\n400\t\n401\t\n402\t(def ^:private wake-value-statuses\n403\t  \"The statuses a woken entry resumes with its poll's own value, by wait\n404\t   reason: ok, end and gap for a parked reader, ok alone for a parked\n405\t   writer -- the write outcome set has no end and no gap, so those\n406\t   keywords on an append are outcomes outside this contract version and\n407\t   refuse. An entry that was never polled carries no status and resumes\n408\t   with the value it already holds.\"\n409\t  {:next #{nil :ok :end :dao.stream/gap}"}
